source: crates/daemon/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Marginalia, a reading app: send an item there to read it with Marginalia's tools, and read the highlights made there back

Usage: mxr reading marginalia [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  status      Whether Marginalia is connected, where, and how many items were sent
  connect     Connect Marginalia: its address, and a personal token from its Account page, Connected apps. The token is read from standard input (or asked for), checked with Marginalia, then kept in the secrets file
  disconnect  Forget Marginalia and remove its token. What was sent stays there
  send        Send an item to Marginalia, or find it there if it was sent before. A digest link's article is fetched first when it isn't saved. --dry-run names what would be sent and where, and contacts nothing
  sync        Read back the highlights made in Marginalia, on one item or on every item sent there. Highlights made in mxr are never changed
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --account <ACCOUNT>  Limit to one account; the default covers every account
      --format <FORMAT>    [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]
  -h, --help               Print help
